Z||000011||Mach10||10-11-2001||11:26 AM||||Uh, that was a little rude... Just 'cos he might not be able to turn a wrench doesn't mean he can't own/upgrade a fiero. You have to learn somewhere...<P>Lotsaballs: Get a pre-88. Easier to find, cheaper to run. Skidpad numbers mean jack-all when slaloming. All it means is how hard the car sticks when going around a 300 ft corner. Weight transfer means more. I can toss my 86 like a banshee around tight corners.<P>In my experience, you can spend less money have more fun with a solid Fiero than a firechicken  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But then, buy a POS from either group, and they'll both give you a black and blue rash on your forehead...||||reg||13
Z||000012||LottaBallsCamaro||10-11-2001||03:19 PM||||Jelly2m8-You can have all the horse power you want, but unless you have room to tub the car out, then you'l be wasting your time on a dragstrip. On a highway, where you start off at 65, thats a different story.<P>revin-I've worked in a shop for 2 years now and do all of my own work. I just recently put a front spindle, axle, all three bearings and seals on my truck. I'm in the middle of replacing an enigine of a 91 lumina 3.1, and I'm building a 400horse 383 for my 91RS, So why dont you go ride a bike son.<P>GTMike, Dennis_6, Mach10, thanks for the helpfull input!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Spektrum-87GT||10-11-2001||04:49 PM||||the fiero has as much potential as you're going to need. The 5 speed getrag transaxle in the 87/88(rare in 86) can handle a LOT of power. <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>   he's run 460+hp engines with no driveline failures. The isuzu 5 speed in other stick shift fieros can handle quite a load too. The only fiero transaxle i've ever heard of going bad because of a v8 was a forum member named tina... some of the other guys can explain to you what exactly happened. i think some kind of abuse was going on(burnouts?) there is also some kind of aftermarket transaxle that will take anything you can throw at it(the tornado?) but its quite expensive, but what high performance transmission isnt? i thought you were talking street cars, are you talking all out drag stip racing here? 600+hp on the street is insane!<BR>I used to go to cnu! I'm 19, and live pretty close to it.||||reg||6
Z||000014||Mach10||10-11-2001||05:57 PM||||Not to start the debate AGAIN, but I don't really believe that any transaxle can handle serious power for extended periods. Having said that, going through one getrag per year would be a decent trade-off for an 11 second Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>But then, as long as you aren't beating on the poor gearbox, there isn't a reason they SHOULD fail. Just be aware that they weren't designed for serious power...||||reg||10
